---
export const prerender = false;
import ProLegalDocument from '../components/ProLegalDocument.astro';
---

<ProLegalDocument
  title="Refund Policy"
  eyebrow="A fair first-purchase promise"
  description="ImageToURL Pro refund and cancellation terms, including a 14-day first-purchase refund."
  intro="Subscriptions should be easy to understand and easy to leave. This policy explains first-purchase refunds, renewals, cancellation, and how to request help."
>
  <section>
    <h2>1. First purchase</h2>
    <p>
      You may request a full refund of your first ImageToURL Pro subscription payment within 14 calendar
      days of purchase. This covers the first monthly or annual payment for a new customer account.
    </p>
    <p>
      Refunds may be denied or limited for fraud, repeated refund abuse, material policy violations, or
      unusually high consumption intended to exploit this offer. Mandatory consumer rights take priority.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>2. Renewals and billing errors</h2>
    <p>
      Renewals are generally non-refundable once a new period starts. If you forgot to cancel, contact us
      within seven days and we will review the request fairly, including use after renewal and applicable
      legal rights.
    </p>
    <p>Verified duplicate, incorrect, or post-cancellation charges will be refunded.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>3. Cancellation</h2>
    <p>
      Canceling through the Paddle portal stops the next renewal. Unless a refund is approved, access
      normally remains active through the paid period and unused time is not automatically prorated.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>4. Requesting a refund</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Visit <a href="https://paddle.net" target="_blank" rel="noopener">paddle.net</a> with the purchase email and transaction details; or</li>
      <li>Email <a href="mailto:blog.boopul@gmail.com?subject=ImageToURL%20Pro%20refund%20request">blog.boopul@gmail.com</a> with your account email, transaction or receipt number, purchase date, and reason.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Never send a full card number or payment password by email.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>5. After a refund</h2>
    <p>
      Paddle returns approved refunds to the original payment method. Processing time depends on the
      payment network. Full refunds may end Pro access immediately, so download important files first.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>6. Consumer rights</h2>
    <p>
      This policy does not remove statutory withdrawal, refund, or consumer-protection rights. If
      Paddle’s buyer terms or applicable law provides stronger rights, those rights apply.
    </p>
  </section>
</ProLegalDocument>
